aml-memory

This project was written for the Agent Memory Leaderboard (AML) Cycle 2, Open-source Methods division.

Prior work whose ideas it builds on (see docs/METHOD_CARD.md for the exact list of borrowed ideas and
every change made):

- imlrz/ReFind (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 ReFind Authors; arXiv:2608.12888) — rendering each turn
  with its UTC timestamp and role, returning neighbouring turns as context, ordering turns by the Add
  ordinal, the reciprocal-rank-fusion idea, and the shape of the service skeleton. No ReFind source
  files are included in this repository.
- FantaSmallhamster/ldbd-sqlite-fts-baseline (no licence published) — the pattern "raw turns in SQLite
  FTS5, BM25 hits, newest turns as a fallback". An early draft of this project (v0.1, commit f09d825)
  contained lines adapted from that file; v0.2 rewrote those modules so that no adapted code remains
  (only names fixed by the API contract and ordinary Python/SQL idioms coincide).
